@@ -45,6 +45,28 @@ npm run build
 `npm run build` bundles the client and performs a Wrangler deployment dry run
 into the ignored `dist/` directory. It does not deploy the site.
 
+## Local article pipeline
+
+Candidate processing is article-first. It collects source pages, sends one
+source-backed writing prompt to the authenticated Codex CLI using
+`gpt-5.6-sol`, accepts plain Markdown, and creates the AI Review package before
+running advisory evidence and style checks. A word-count miss, missing inline
+link, imperfect Markdown wrapper, or failed advisory rule does not block the
+article from review.
+
+The local controller account must be signed in to Codex. When its launch
+environment has a limited `PATH`, set `ANYWAYS_CODEX_BIN` to the absolute Codex
+CLI path. The model, reasoning effort, and timeout are configurable through the
+variables documented in `.env.example`.
+
+```sh
+npm run pipeline:process -- <candidate-id>
+```
+
+The older structured-output harness remains available only as
+`npm run pipeline:legacy-structured -- <input.json>` for regression and
+comparison work. It is not the newsroom delivery path.
+
