+{
+  "attempt": 1,
+  "raw_response": "{\"headline\": \"Why Are Physical Menus and Printed Zines Becoming Status Symbols in a Digital Age?\",\"dek\": \"From Quo Vadis' illustrated pie menus to Hato Press' collectible zines, print media is making a comeback as a symbol of authenticity and artistic value.\",\"body_markdown\": \"In an age dominated by digital screens and instant access, physical menus and printed zines are experiencing a renaissance, becoming coveted status symbols among creatives and consumers alike. This resurgence is not just a nostalgic throwback—it reflects a deeper cultural shift toward valuing authenticity, craftsmanship, and collectibility in an increasingly virtual world.\\n\\n### The Art of the Menu\\nAt Quo Vadis, a London-based restaurant, the menu is more than a list of dishes—it's a work of art. The 'Pie of the Day' is highlighted with a unique John Broadley illustration, and the menu itself is designed to reflect the restaurant's commitment to traditional British cuisine. Chef Jeremy Lee emphasizes the use of all kitchen produce, including scraps for stocks, reinforcing the idea that food, like print media, is best when made with care and intention. This attention to detail extends to Lee's book, *Cooking: Simply and Well, for One or Many*, which features a whole chapter on pies, showcasing the enduring appeal of the humble pie.\\n\\n### The Resurgence of Print\\nPrint media, once thought to be on the brink of extinction, is making a strong comeback. i-D magazine, which had been absent from UK newsstands since 2023 due to Vice's bankruptcy, has returned under the ownership of Karlie Kloss through her Bedford Media conglomerate. This revival is tied to a renewed interest in luxury and indie titles, as Gen Z, in particular, seeks out tangible, nostalgic experiences that digital media cannot replicate.\\n\\n### Zines: The Cool Factor\\nZines, small-circulation self-published works, have long been a staple of the creative industry, offering an alternative to mainstream glossy magazines. Independent publications like *OOMK*, *The Chapess*, and *Diaspora Drama* have provided a platform for emerging voices and artistic experimentation. Today, zines are more than just a medium—they are a status symbol, with collectibility and artistic value driving their appeal. Hato Press, for example, recently launched its 50th zine with an exhibition showcasing all artist editions since 2020. These zines are Risograph-printed and part of an ongoing series with no creative constraints, making them highly sought after by collectors and art enthusiasts.\\n\\n### The Future of Print\\nAs the creative industry continues to evolve, the value of print media is being redefined. Whether it's a beautifully illustrated menu or a hand-printed zine, these physical artifacts are not just relics of the past—they are symbols of a future where authenticity and craftsmanship are celebrated. In a world where everything is digital, the tangible becomes the rare, and the rare becomes the valuable.\",\"claim_to_source\": [{\"claim\": \"Quo Vadis features a 'Pie of the Day' with a fixed price of £19.50, highlighted on the menu with a John Broadley illustration.\",\"source_ids\": [\"source:a3a957f59e18dd4b54904fa250f129af3927a572c0bda8e1fb4400a6c4ef298e:17f94a5e-25e8-4ae7-b1d7-add0303ad31e:2\"]},{\"claim\": \"Jeremy Lee emphasizes the traditional value of pies, using all kitchen produce and scraps for stocks.\",\"source_ids\": [\"source:a3a957f59e18dd4b54904fa250f129af3927a572c0bda8e1fb4400a6c4ef298e:17f94a5e-25e8-4ae7-b1d7-add0303ad31e:2\"]},{\"claim\": \"Pies are highlighted in Lee's book 'Cooking: Simply and Well, for One or Many' with various recipes.\",\"source_ids\": [\"source:a3a957f59e18dd4b54904fa250f129af3927a572c0bda8e1fb4400a6c4ef298e:17f94a5e-25e8-4ae7-b1d7-add0303ad31e:2\"]},{\"claim\": \"Quo Vadis offers an affordable pie option with a focus on seasonal and traditional British cuisine.\",\"source_ids\": [\"source:a3a957f59e18dd4b54904fa250f129af39